claim.claim-text:
receiving, from a network node of an access network (104), a request to transition from a radio resource control, RRC, connected state to a RRC inactive state and context information indicating one or more_logical channels, LCHs or radio bearers, that remain available for uplink, UL, transmission while in the RRC inactive state;
transitioning to the RRC inactive state ;  with respect to the network node (104) and
on condition that UL data associated with the indicated one or more LCHs or radio bearers becomes available for transmission, a validity timer associated with resources for data transfer is running, and the UL data satisfies one or more criteria for transmission while in the RRC inactive state, transmitting the UL data and an identity of the WTRU while in the RRC inactive state, wherein the one or more criteria for transmission comprises a criterion such that an amount of the UL data is less than a threshold.

a criterion that a size of an available UL grant can accommodate the amount of the UL data;
a criterion that the WTRU is within a dynamically configured logical area; and
a criterion that the WTRU is within a semi-static configured area.

communicating with a first transmit receive point, TRP;
determining, autonomously, in the RRC inactive state to engage in mobility between the first TRP and a second TRP based on a condition; and
moving, autonomously, in the RRC inactive state from the first TRP to the second TRP upon an occurrence of the condition.

a determination of an availability of a more suitable cell associated with the second TRP relative to a current cell associated with the first TRP from a link quality perspective;
a determination of an availability of a more suitable cell associated with the second TRP relative to a current cell associated with the first TRP from a service perspective;
a determination of an availability of a more suitable cell associated with the second TRP relative to a current cell associated with the first TRP from a resource availability perspective; and
a determination of an availability of a more suitable cell associated with the second TRP relative to a current cell associated with the first TRP from a capability perspective.
